From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Cui <bh@bugs.cc>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:13:31 -0400
Subject: feat: add a refresh command that fetches usage now, one account at a
 time
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`cswap list` serves the cached measurement while an account is inside
the serve TTL, its poll plan, or a failure backoff. After a usage
endpoint 429 the backoff honors Retry-After plus a margin, which is an
hour or more of "· 1h ago" on the listing with no command that asks
again. Both accounts sharing one token's budget made this visible:
identical numbers on both rows, both parked until the same minute.

`cswap refresh [num|email ...]` fetches the given accounts (default:
all) right now. UsageStore.reserve grows a `force` mode that skips the
freshness, poll-plan and backoff gates while keeping the two that make
a request pointless or unsafe: a dead refresh token, and another
collector's live lease. Every account is claimed, fetched and recorded
on its own, so a 429 on one never blocks the others; a rate-limited
account prints the server's own Retry-After deadline (the local backoff
when the server sent none) and keeps its last measurement on screen.
Exit code 1 when any requested account could not be refreshed.

